","Above the world average: 5%–19% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2021 (19%).","Not cited: on average 34% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 4 of 4 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2019: mean 0.52, median 0.18, top work 4.67. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2016–2018, 2022 and 2024–2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2014 has fewer than 10 works (2014: 2), too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2015–2023 have a median of 3–6 citations each; the highest median (6) is in 2020.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2015 have at least 21.2 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2025–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 5 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2019: mean 7.9, median 4, top work 58. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2016–2018, 2022 and 2024–2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2014 has fewer than 10 works (2014: 2), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}